30-Second Senior Developer Interview Answer

We package the Spring Boot application as a JAR, create a Docker image, and push it to ECR. 
In ECS, we create a Cluster, Task Definition, and Service. The Task Definition contains image URI,
CPU, memory, ports, environment variables, Execution Role, and Task Role. The Service maintains 
the desired number of tasks and is attached to an ALB. The ALB routes traffic to ECS tasks and performs health checks. 
CloudWatch captures application logs, while auto-scaling can increase or decrease task count based on CPU or memory usage.
